e mention a class. Do not let the category semantics of the head noun pull the label toward **DiseaseClass**. **Negative constraint:** This does NOT apply when the noun phrase enumerates or quantifies over multiple distinct disorders, or when it functions as a generic kind-level term, such as a phenotype or feature term characterizing a syndrome class across a population. In those cases, keep **DiseaseClass**. Modifier spans within the mention do not change the referential decision for the head.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2450, "output_tokens": 2198, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 1862}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}